<para id="RM00000064B00GX" category="C" type-id="302FB" name-id="5914Y-00" from="200708" to="200810">
<dtccode>P0571/52</dtccode>
<dtcname>STP Light SW System (Cruise)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0571/76</dtccode>
<dtcname>STP Light SW System (Cruise)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000064B00GX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CAU00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The stop light switch assembly outputs the brake pedal operation signal to the engine control computer. Using this signal, the engine control computer performs cruise control cancel control.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Description</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0571/52</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>IG ON, cruise control main switch ON</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Input signal from the stop light switch is abnormal</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Fuse (STOP, IGN)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Stop Light Switch Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector (stop light signal circuit)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>P0571/76</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>During cruise control (vehicle-to-vehicle distance control mode)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>With the IG1 terminal voltage at 11 to 14 V, there is no input signal at the STP terminal when the BRAKE LP relay drive output (STP0) is ON, or with the IG1 terminal voltage at 11 to 14 V, the input signals of the STP and STP2 terminals differ when the BRAKE LP relay drive output (STP0) is OFF</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Fuse (STOP, ECU-IG No,1)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>BRAKE LP Relay</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector (battery - BRAKE LP relay)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector (BRAKE LP relay - ABS &amp; traction actuator assembly)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>ABS &amp; Traction Actuator Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
